<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">18 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 18 April, from 796 to 1955.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">796</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">King Æthelred I of Northumbria is murdered</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Æthelred I was killed at Corbridge by his own nobles. His death, typical of Northumbria's violent politics, came three years after Viking raiders had sacked the monastery at Lindisfarne.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1506</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Julius II lays the foundation stone of the new St Peter's</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pope Julius II laid the first stone of Bramante's new basilica in Rome. Building took 120 years and drew on Michelangelo, Maderno and Bernini.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1775</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Paul Revere rides to warn of British troops</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Paul Revere and William Dawes rode from Boston to warn that British regulars were marching to seize colonial arms. The first shots of the Revolutionary War were fired at dawn the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1906</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Earthquake and fire devastate San Francisco</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A magnitude 7.9 earthquake struck before dawn, and fires burned for three days. Some 3,000 people died and more than half the city's population was left homeless.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1923</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Yankee Stadium opens with a Babe Ruth home run</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Babe Ruth hit a three-run home run in the first game at the new Bronx ballpark, quickly nicknamed 'The House That Ruth Built'. It was home to the Yankees until 2008.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1955</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Albert Einstein dies in Princeton</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Albert Einstein died aged 76. His theories of special and general relativity and his work on light quanta transformed physics in the twentieth century.</p></li></ol>
